<title>PHILIPPINES: RFC buys into local bank for 45 mln pesos.</title>
<headline>RFC buys into local bank for 45 mln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial company RFC Inc said on Monday it had consummated the 30 percent buy-in of Unitrust Development Bank for 45 million pesos.</p>
<p>RFC corporate secretary Mario Lorenzo said RFC had bought 450,000 common shares. RFC remained unchanged at 25 pesos on Monday after rising from six pesos since February 17.</p>
<p>RFC is controlled by Grogram Ltd, a unit of MBf Holdings Bhd of Malaysia.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
